      {
        "finding": "Penultimate features and the classifier align strongly at subspace level (Level-2 z-scores 43–1341 across ResNet, ConvNeXt, MLP-Mixer and ViT-Tiny). Basis-level (Level-3) alignment is degenerate or near zero, and the commutator is nonzero in ReLU MLPs but zero in linear ones.",
        "proposed_claim": "Within a network, feature–classifier alignment holds at subspace level but not at basis level in nonlinear networks.",
        "row_ids": []
      }
    ],
    "controls": "y",
    "capability_check": "n",
