    "code_released": "not stated",
    "peer_reviewed": "preprint",
    "problems": "The head-overlap experiments are terminal-state observations without training checkpoints, so they do not establish dynamics. The Haar baseline controls for subspace dimension but not Transformer training objectives; the authors note that another trained model could also show excess overlap. The aggregate overlap cannot distinguish a few nearly identical heads from many partially overlapping heads. No capability measure is reported.",
    "rows_left_out": "No head-overlap results were omitted. The within-network classifier–feature alignment and activation-commutator results in Section 7.1 and Appendix E.1 were not included as rows because they measure a different internal alignment construct rather than cross-model representation convergence.",
